        "text": "name: Node CLI tests\non:\n  pull_request:\n    paths:\n      - 'skills/**'\n      - 'tests/**'\n      - 'package.json'\n  workflow_dispatch:\npermissions:\n  contents: read\nconcurrency:\n  group: node-cli-tests-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: true\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 5\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: '22'\n      - run: npm test\n"
      },
      {
        "path": "spec/spec-process-cicd-node-cli-tests.md",
        "sha256": "ba041878609f856cf1940bc847c2efc5a9e6860422a84a21afae233bfffe8931",
        "text": "---\ntitle: Node CLI test workflow specification\nversion: 1.0\ndate_created: 2026-11-08\ntags: [node, unit-tests, github-actions]\n---\n\n## Workflow behavior\n\nThe validation job runs the Node CLI regression suite for pull requests touching `skills/**`, `tests/**` or `package.json`. Maintainers may also dispatch it manually. Each run tests one checkout with Node.js 22 on a GitHub-hosted Linux runner.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Matching PR or manual dispatch] --> B[Prepare checkout and runtime]\n    B --> C{Regression suite passes}\n    C -->|Yes| D[Success]\n    C -->|No| E[Failure]\n```\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance check |\n| --- | --- |\n| Trigger scope | A docs-only pull request does not start validation. A test change qualifies. |\n| Token access | The job has repository contents read access. It consumes no configured secrets. |\n| Runtime | The job times out after 5 minutes. A newer run for the same ref cancels a superseded validation. |\n| Result | The test exit status determines the job result. The workflow defines no build artifacts or deployment. |\n\nUse failing test names and logs to diagnose the run locally before any retry. The fixture defines no automatic retry or deployment job.\n"
      }
    ],
